What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<device>/pen_type
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		The active stylus the touch controller firmware senses, as
		the stock Android driver numbers them in its pencil_connected
		node:

		== ==================================================
		0  no stylus: the firmware does not look for one
		1  the default stylus (the OnePlus Pad 3's own)
		2  stylus type 2
		3  stylus type 3
		4  stylus type 4
		5  stylus type 5
		== ==================================================

		It starts at the novatek,pen-type of the device tree. The
		firmware is told the value each time it starts (at boot, at
		resume, after a controller reset) and at once on a write while
		the display is on. While the display is off it only waits for
		a double tap and is told that there is no stylus.

		A write fails with EIO when the firmware did not take the
		command; the value is kept and sent again at the next resume.

		Present only on controllers described with novatek,pen-type.

		Access: Read, Write
		Valid values: 0 to 5
